1
00:00:01,875 --> 00:00:03,208
[wilting]

2
00:00:05,666 --> 00:00:08,125
[growling exhale]

3
00:00:08,125 --> 00:00:09,833
[chittering]

4
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:11,083
[roaring]

5
00:00:11,083 --> 00:00:12,541
[chittering]

6
00:00:12,541 --> 00:00:13,500
[shrieking]

7
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,500
[roaring]

8
00:00:19,625 --> 00:00:20,541
[Arin grunts]

9
00:00:20,541 --> 00:00:21,500
[Arin] Sorry
hanging out with us

10
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:22,500
got you into this.

11
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:23,625
[Euphrasia grunts]

12
00:00:23,625 --> 00:00:25,500
I'm ready
to write this destiny with you,

13
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,416
however it turns out.

14
00:00:31,333 --> 00:00:33,291
[snarling]

15
00:00:37,708 --> 00:00:41,833
<i>[telepathically]</i>
<i>The time... has come.</i>

16
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:44,791
<i>Thank you, Titanium Ninja.</i>

17
00:00:44,791 --> 00:00:47,500
<i>May our souls meet</i>
<i>in the next cycle.</i>

18
00:00:49,125 --> 00:00:51,375
[Zane] No, not yet!

19
00:00:51,375 --> 00:00:52,833
Trust in Lloyd.

20
00:00:53,833 --> 00:00:54,833
H'yah!

21
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:56,083
There's fight left in us!

22
00:00:56,083 --> 00:00:57,000
Ah!

23
00:00:58,250 --> 00:00:59,666
Huah!

24
00:00:59,666 --> 00:01:01,750
[monsters snarling]

25
00:01:04,583 --> 00:01:06,458
[whispers echoing]

26
00:01:07,458 --> 00:01:09,458
[gasping]

27
00:01:09,458 --> 00:01:10,500
What was that?

28
00:01:12,166 --> 00:01:14,125
[whispers becoming louder]

29
00:01:18,250 --> 00:01:19,333
[together] Lloyd?

30
00:01:19,333 --> 00:01:20,250
[roaring]

31
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:22,166
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

32
00:01:22,166 --> 00:01:23,375
♪ So much to see ♪

33
00:01:23,375 --> 00:01:26,166
♪ Jump up, kick back
whip around and spin ♪

34
00:01:26,166 --> 00:01:27,875
♪ Together we will rise ♪

35
00:01:27,875 --> 00:01:29,291
♪ Whip around and spin ♪

36
00:01:29,291 --> 00:01:31,000
♪ Together we will rise ♪

37
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,875
♪ For what's right ♪

38
00:01:35,291 --> 00:01:37,708
[♪♪♪]

39
00:01:40,625 --> 00:01:44,291
Several grid problems
in sectors 7, 9, and 14-Alpha.

40
00:01:44,291 --> 00:01:45,250
[heavy thudding]

41
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:46,291
[gasping]

42
00:01:46,291 --> 00:01:47,416
[screeching overhead]

43
00:01:49,041 --> 00:01:50,750
Another monster?

44
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:51,958
We still haven't
finished repairs

45
00:01:51,958 --> 00:01:54,083
from the last attack.

46
00:01:55,833 --> 00:01:58,458
It's... not a monster.

47
00:01:58,458 --> 00:02:00,666
Wrong. It's the worst monster

48
00:02:00,666 --> 00:02:03,000
Imperium has ever known.

49
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,750
[♪♪♪]

50
00:02:12,541 --> 00:02:15,291
<i>[Empress Beatrix]</i>
<i>People of Imperium!</i>

51
00:02:15,291 --> 00:02:17,291
<i>My people!</i>

52
00:02:17,291 --> 00:02:20,250
<i>Who represents you</i>
<i>in my absence?</i>

53
00:02:21,666 --> 00:02:23,666
I am a duly elected official.

54
00:02:24,666 --> 00:02:26,666
<i>Aren't you that boy</i>

55
00:02:26,666 --> 00:02:29,458
<i>who once brought me</i>
<i>a baby dragon?</i>

56
00:02:29,458 --> 00:02:31,583
<i>You dreamt of nothing more</i>

57
00:02:31,583 --> 00:02:34,625
<i>than serving me</i>
<i>as one of my Claws!</i>

58
00:02:34,625 --> 00:02:37,041
That was a long time ago,

59
00:02:37,041 --> 00:02:40,291
when I was brainwashed
by your propaganda,

60
00:02:40,291 --> 00:02:41,708
but I woke up.

61
00:02:41,708 --> 00:02:44,166
All of the people of Imperium
woke up.

62
00:02:44,166 --> 00:02:46,166
We saw who you really are--

63
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:48,583
a tyrant who lied
about safe energy

64
00:02:48,583 --> 00:02:51,375
while running secret
dragon-draining chambers!

65
00:02:51,375 --> 00:02:53,708
[Beatrix] I drained
those disgusting dragons

66
00:02:53,708 --> 00:02:56,041
to keep my kingdom prosperous.

67
00:02:56,041 --> 00:02:58,916
I hear your "free society"

68
00:02:58,916 --> 00:03:01,791
<i>can barely keep the lights on.</i>

69
00:03:01,791 --> 00:03:05,416
<i>The lives of Imperium Citizens</i>
<i>were perfect</i>

70
00:03:05,416 --> 00:03:08,291
<i>when the rightful ruler</i>
<i>was on her throne!</i>

71
00:03:08,291 --> 00:03:11,250
You lied, and hurt,
and oppressed the people.

72
00:03:11,250 --> 00:03:13,541
Our new Imperium has struggles,

73
00:03:13,541 --> 00:03:14,625
but we work hard

74
00:03:14,625 --> 00:03:16,875
to make our city
function independently,

75
00:03:16,875 --> 00:03:19,083
without harming other beings!

76
00:03:19,083 --> 00:03:20,750
<i>[sighing]</i>

77
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:22,916
<i>My subjects!</i>

78
00:03:22,916 --> 00:03:27,166
<i>You all once hailed me</i>
<i>as your Good Empress.</i>

79
00:03:27,166 --> 00:03:29,416
<i>Despite your betrayal,</i>

80
00:03:29,416 --> 00:03:32,541
<i>I will give you one chance</i>
<i>to surrender</i>

81
00:03:32,541 --> 00:03:35,291
<i>and receive mercy,</i>

82
00:03:35,291 --> 00:03:39,125
<i>or else I will take Imperium</i>
<i>by force,</i>

83
00:03:39,125 --> 00:03:41,291
<i>and there will be no mercy!</i>

84
00:03:42,541 --> 00:03:44,708
I know where I stand.

85
00:03:44,708 --> 00:03:47,708
Being ruled by tyrants
was the old way,

86
00:03:47,708 --> 00:03:49,708
but it's not about what I want.

87
00:03:49,708 --> 00:03:52,750
We decide
by the voice of the people.

88
00:03:52,750 --> 00:03:56,500
All who wish to open the doors
to Beatrix, speak!

89
00:03:59,458 --> 00:04:01,333
All who wish to stand firm

90
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:02,833
for the freedom of Imperium

91
00:04:02,833 --> 00:04:04,166
and refuse her,

92
00:04:04,166 --> 00:04:06,416
no matter what
she may throw at us?

93
00:04:06,416 --> 00:04:08,166
[all cheering]

94
00:04:09,875 --> 00:04:13,208
Former Empress,
the people have spoken.

95
00:04:13,208 --> 00:04:15,500
Imperium rejects you.

96
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:16,375
Again.

97
00:04:16,375 --> 00:04:19,583
<i>Then you choose "no mercy"?</i>

98
00:04:19,583 --> 00:04:21,333
<i>Good.</i>

99
00:04:21,333 --> 00:04:24,416
<i>That's a much more</i>
<i>satisfying option...</i>

100
00:04:24,416 --> 00:04:26,208
<i>for me.</i>

101
00:04:26,208 --> 00:04:29,333
If you step foot
within these walls,

102
00:04:29,333 --> 00:04:30,541
you will be arrested

103
00:04:30,541 --> 00:04:33,583
and prosecuted in a fair trial
for your crimes,

104
00:04:33,583 --> 00:04:35,666
including the death
of your father,

105
00:04:35,666 --> 00:04:37,916
Emperor Levo Vespasian-Orus!

106
00:04:37,916 --> 00:04:39,375
<i>[laughing]</i>

107
00:04:39,375 --> 00:04:42,666
<i>Remember,</i>
<i>despite my better judgment,</i>

108
00:04:42,666 --> 00:04:46,208
<i>I gave you a chance for peace.</i>

109
00:04:46,208 --> 00:04:49,500
<i>What happens next</i>
<i>is on your heads!</i>

110
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:51,916
Time to rise and shine!

111
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:53,458
[weapon blasting]

112
00:04:55,666 --> 00:04:56,791
[monsters snarling]

113
00:04:58,166 --> 00:05:02,333
[roaring]

114
00:05:04,666 --> 00:05:05,833
[frightened murmuring]

115
00:05:05,833 --> 00:05:07,916
Our walls can't hold
against all that.

116
00:05:07,916 --> 00:05:10,416
Have we made a mistake?

117
00:05:10,416 --> 00:05:11,583
Ninja!

118
00:05:11,583 --> 00:05:13,833
This is why I kept you alive

119
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:16,375
in such a humiliating state.

120
00:05:16,375 --> 00:05:19,916
So you can helplessly
witness my triumph.

121
00:05:19,916 --> 00:05:21,458
[groaning]

122
00:05:21,458 --> 00:05:24,125
Now to take back what's mine.

123
00:05:24,125 --> 00:05:26,375
March on Imperium!

124
00:05:26,375 --> 00:05:28,833
[roaring]

125
00:05:28,833 --> 00:05:32,500
[♪♪♪]

126
00:05:39,166 --> 00:05:40,333
[Lloyd] Raah!

127
00:05:41,833 --> 00:05:43,750
[monsters snarling]

128
00:05:46,208 --> 00:05:47,250
[Lloyd] Raah!

129
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:53,041
[♪♪♪]

130
00:05:59,458 --> 00:06:02,375
I didn't know he could get
all dragony like that.

131
00:06:02,375 --> 00:06:03,791
[Arin] He can't,

132
00:06:03,791 --> 00:06:05,791
or he... couldn't.

133
00:06:05,791 --> 00:06:06,958
[wind gusting]

134
00:06:06,958 --> 00:06:08,666
-[Arin] Look!
-Huh?

135
00:06:08,666 --> 00:06:11,125
Looks like the end
of our destiny

136
00:06:11,125 --> 00:06:13,333
hasn't been written after all!

137
00:06:13,333 --> 00:06:14,875
Ninja... go!

138
00:06:15,916 --> 00:06:19,166
[♪♪♪]

139
00:06:19,166 --> 00:06:20,875
[snarling

140
00:06:20,875 --> 00:06:22,000
[♪♪♪]

141
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:40,875
[Lloyd] H'yah!

142
00:06:45,666 --> 00:06:48,208
Huh?

143
00:06:52,625 --> 00:06:54,333
How did you stabilize
our powers--

144
00:06:54,333 --> 00:06:56,791
You're a dragon now? How?

145
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:58,041
-Why--
-Nice tail!

146
00:06:58,041 --> 00:06:59,250
I've always wanted one.

147
00:06:59,250 --> 00:07:00,583
[Lloyd] Slow down.

148
00:07:00,583 --> 00:07:02,166
One at a time.

149
00:07:02,166 --> 00:07:04,125
I already hear so much,

150
00:07:04,125 --> 00:07:06,208
feel so much...

151
00:07:06,208 --> 00:07:08,166
The lean of a tree,

152
00:07:08,166 --> 00:07:09,750
the growth of the grass...

153
00:07:09,750 --> 00:07:12,750
<i>[telepathically]</i>
<i>It is overwhelming at first.</i>

154
00:07:12,750 --> 00:07:15,416
<i>Be patient. Be present.</i>

155
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
[breathing deeply]

156
00:07:22,041 --> 00:07:24,916
<i>Your friends' hope</i>
<i>was not false.</i>

157
00:07:24,916 --> 00:07:28,750
<i>The Legend of the Green Ninja</i>
<i>continues in you,</i>

158
00:07:28,750 --> 00:07:32,083
<i>yet the form you've taken...</i>

159
00:07:32,083 --> 00:07:34,291
<i>I've never seen</i>
<i>the likes of it before</i>

160
00:07:34,291 --> 00:07:35,750
<i>in a Green Ninja.</i>

161
00:07:35,750 --> 00:07:39,125
Why would I be the first
to take a new form?

162
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:42,916
<i>Your life experiences,</i>
<i>your connections...</i>

163
00:07:42,916 --> 00:07:45,625
<i>I feared they would</i>
<i>bring you down,</i>

164
00:07:45,625 --> 00:07:46,958
<i>but perhaps they led you</i>

165
00:07:46,958 --> 00:07:49,416
<i>to unlock</i>
<i>this part of your being.</i>

166
00:07:49,416 --> 00:07:53,166
Ah, my head...
these feelings...

167
00:07:53,166 --> 00:07:54,625
Can I turn them down?

168
00:07:54,625 --> 00:07:57,791
<i>You are connected</i>
<i>to life itself now.</i>

169
00:07:57,791 --> 00:08:00,666
<i>It cannot be turned down,</i>

170
00:08:00,666 --> 00:08:03,625
<i>but you can rise to meet it.</i>

171
00:08:03,625 --> 00:08:06,750
It's... so strange.

172
00:08:06,750 --> 00:08:08,875
<i>Life is strange.</i>

173
00:08:08,875 --> 00:08:11,791
<i>Life is also ordinary.</i>

174
00:08:11,791 --> 00:08:15,083
<i>Life is so many things.</i>

175
00:08:15,083 --> 00:08:16,291
<i>I will miss it.</i>

176
00:08:16,291 --> 00:08:17,875
[groaning softly]

177
00:08:17,875 --> 00:08:19,625
Why aren't they better?

178
00:08:19,625 --> 00:08:22,000
I thought the ritual
would fix everything.

179
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,708
It... it should have,

180
00:08:24,708 --> 00:08:26,333
but I sense...

181
00:08:26,333 --> 00:08:28,750
something out there

182
00:08:28,750 --> 00:08:31,875
manipulating
unbalanced source energy,

183
00:08:31,875 --> 00:08:33,875
draining the Wood,

184
00:08:33,875 --> 00:08:35,333
even though it's distant.

185
00:08:35,333 --> 00:08:36,500
What is it?

186
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:37,833
A Source Dragon?

187
00:08:37,833 --> 00:08:38,875
Ras?

188
00:08:38,875 --> 00:08:40,291
No.

189
00:08:40,291 --> 00:08:42,000
An artifact, maybe,

190
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,958
or a weapon?

191
00:08:43,958 --> 00:08:46,416
It's more than just a weapon.

192
00:08:46,416 --> 00:08:47,916
It's evil.

193
00:08:47,916 --> 00:08:50,541
To save the Whispering Wood,
I have to stop it.

194
00:08:50,541 --> 00:08:51,583
No.

195
00:08:51,583 --> 00:08:53,666
<i>We </i>have to stop it.

196
00:08:53,666 --> 00:08:54,916
Sign me up,

197
00:08:54,916 --> 00:08:57,625
but how can we find this thing?

198
00:08:57,625 --> 00:08:59,250
Lloyd, can you lead us there?

199
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:02,041
I just... don't know.

200
00:09:02,041 --> 00:09:03,791
[marching feet]

201
00:09:03,791 --> 00:09:05,958
[♪♪♪]

202
00:09:15,166 --> 00:09:16,625
[grunting with effort]

203
00:09:16,625 --> 00:09:17,625
[rumbling]

204
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,416
[grunting]

205
00:09:21,416 --> 00:09:22,375
[panting]

206
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:27,083
[rumbling]

207
00:09:27,083 --> 00:09:28,125
Aah!

208
00:09:28,125 --> 00:09:29,500
[groaning]

209
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:31,375
[weapons powering up]

210
00:09:31,375 --> 00:09:32,583
Sorry, had to.

211
00:09:32,583 --> 00:09:34,000
Wrists were getting
a little sore.

212
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:37,583
[♪♪♪]

213
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:45,000
-[Cole] Yaah!
-[Beatrix] How?

214
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,666
[LaRow yelps]

215
00:09:47,666 --> 00:09:48,750
Oof!

216
00:09:51,375 --> 00:09:53,916
That's not for you, whelp!

217
00:09:53,916 --> 00:09:55,000
H'yah!

218
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,750
[Cole] I just need
to touch it once...

219
00:09:57,750 --> 00:09:58,750
[grunting]

220
00:10:00,833 --> 00:10:02,375
[♪♪♪]

221
00:10:06,791 --> 00:10:07,625
Yaah!

222
00:10:08,958 --> 00:10:10,583
[Beatrix] Aah!

223
00:10:10,583 --> 00:10:12,291
Huah! Oh!

224
00:10:12,291 --> 00:10:13,541
[clanging]

225
00:10:13,541 --> 00:10:15,458
[snarling]

226
00:10:15,458 --> 00:10:17,708
[roaring]

227
00:10:18,875 --> 00:10:21,250
[Cole] You've caused Imperium
enough trouble.

228
00:10:21,250 --> 00:10:22,666
Let's wrap this up!

229
00:10:22,666 --> 00:10:25,791
[Beatrix] I will not
be insulted by an outlander!

230
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:28,166
[monsters roaring]

231
00:10:30,333 --> 00:10:31,375
[Beatrix] Attack!

232
00:10:31,375 --> 00:10:33,500
[monsters roaring]

233
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:35,750
[Cole] Aah! Yaah!

234
00:10:37,041 --> 00:10:39,541
[rumbling]

235
00:10:41,166 --> 00:10:42,416
Haah! Raah! Yaah!

236
00:10:43,791 --> 00:10:44,791
[grunting]

237
00:10:44,791 --> 00:10:48,458
Ugh, this could not be
more gross!

238
00:10:48,458 --> 00:10:51,083
[Beatrix] A minor distraction.

239
00:10:51,083 --> 00:10:52,666
Scale the wall!

240
00:10:52,666 --> 00:10:54,583
[monsters hissing]

241
00:10:57,375 --> 00:10:59,375
We've gotta get
the Electro-Barrier back up!

242
00:10:59,375 --> 00:11:02,041
You ordered us to shut it down
to conserve energy.

243
00:11:02,041 --> 00:11:04,791
We re-routed
every single power cell.

244
00:11:04,791 --> 00:11:05,666
How could we--?

245
00:11:05,666 --> 00:11:07,166
We find a way!

246
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:09,041
The Elemental Master of Earth
is risking his life

247
00:11:09,041 --> 00:11:11,208
because he hasn't
given up on us,

248
00:11:11,208 --> 00:11:13,000
so we can't give up either.

249
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,375
Let's go!

250
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:19,083
H'ah! H'yah!

251
00:11:19,083 --> 00:11:20,083
R'ah!

252
00:11:21,083 --> 00:11:22,250
[car horn plays
"La Cucaracha"]

253
00:11:22,250 --> 00:11:25,166
[engine revving]

254
00:11:25,166 --> 00:11:26,166
[Kai] Ha ha!

255
00:11:26,166 --> 00:11:27,916
Knew if we followed
these masked jerks

256
00:11:27,916 --> 00:11:29,041
we'd find something fun!

257
00:11:29,041 --> 00:11:31,708
[Cole] Jay? Nya? Kai?

258
00:11:31,708 --> 00:11:34,166
[Jay] Get off Cole, you freaks!

259
00:11:34,166 --> 00:11:35,791
Uh, that is Cole, right?

260
00:11:35,791 --> 00:11:37,166
I haven't gotten back

261
00:11:37,166 --> 00:11:39,458
any memories of him
looking like that.

262
00:11:41,708 --> 00:11:45,125
[Nya] I'm, like,
95 to 98% sure that's him.

263
00:11:45,125 --> 00:11:46,083
There she is,

264
00:11:46,083 --> 00:11:47,375
and that must be the weapon

265
00:11:47,375 --> 00:11:49,208
her goons were talking about.

266
00:11:49,208 --> 00:11:50,750
We got here too late.

267
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:52,625
[Kai] Told ya
you should've let me drive.

268
00:11:52,625 --> 00:11:54,708
[Jay scoffs]
My driving is great!

269
00:11:54,708 --> 00:11:55,958
[tires squealing]

270
00:11:55,958 --> 00:11:57,708
[Kai] Yeah, real great!

271
00:12:00,375 --> 00:12:01,541
[Jay] Better than the time

272
00:12:01,541 --> 00:12:03,958
you melted the Land Bounty's
steering wheel!

273
00:12:03,958 --> 00:12:05,375
[Kai] Can we lose
this guy's memories again?

274
00:12:05,375 --> 00:12:07,166
[Jay] Hold tight!

275
00:12:07,166 --> 00:12:08,250
[tires squealing]

276
00:12:11,166 --> 00:12:12,375
[snarling]

277
00:12:12,375 --> 00:12:13,666
[Nya] Jay, hit the thing!

278
00:12:17,166 --> 00:12:18,166
Now we're talkin'!

279
00:12:18,166 --> 00:12:19,875
[roaring]

280
00:12:19,875 --> 00:12:21,083
[♪♪♪]

281
00:12:23,583 --> 00:12:24,791
[Jay] Whoo-hoo!

282
00:12:24,791 --> 00:12:27,125
Racer Mode was my best idea yet!

283
00:12:27,125 --> 00:12:28,666
[Nya] It was my idea!

284
00:12:28,666 --> 00:12:31,708
[Jay] As the love of your life,
I'm sure I inspired it.

285
00:12:31,708 --> 00:12:33,958
[Nya] You told me repeatedly
not to do it

286
00:12:33,958 --> 00:12:34,916
'cause we'd never use it...

287
00:12:34,916 --> 00:12:36,083
[monster roaring]

288
00:12:36,083 --> 00:12:37,791
...which just made me
want to do it more.

289
00:12:37,791 --> 00:12:41,416
[Jay] Exactly! I'm a master
of reverse inspiration.

290
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,958
Lifting 88A, Side 2,
on your mark.

291
00:12:48,958 --> 00:12:50,166
Mark!

292
00:12:51,583 --> 00:12:52,958
Feed it in.

293
00:12:55,750 --> 00:12:58,500
[powering up]

294
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:04,541
Yes!

295
00:13:04,541 --> 00:13:06,500
[♪♪♪]

296
00:13:08,166 --> 00:13:09,666
[monsters snarling]

297
00:13:09,666 --> 00:13:10,541
[♪♪♪]

298
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:14,750
No!

299
00:13:14,750 --> 00:13:16,208
They will not keep me out!

300
00:13:20,458 --> 00:13:21,958
[gasping] Oh no!

301
00:13:21,958 --> 00:13:25,291
Empress, we have several
covert Loyalists still inside.

302
00:13:25,291 --> 00:13:27,291
Looks like
they've sabotaged the barrier.

303
00:13:27,291 --> 00:13:29,250
[Beatrix] When we
take back the kingdom,

304
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:31,958
remind me to spare them
from my wrath.

305
00:13:35,458 --> 00:13:36,541
[alert tones beeping]

306
00:13:36,541 --> 00:13:38,875
The barrier is turning off!

307
00:13:41,833 --> 00:13:43,666
[Nya] Their barrier failed!

308
00:13:43,666 --> 00:13:44,750
[tires squealing]

309
00:13:44,750 --> 00:13:46,583
[Jay] They probably
could use the help

310
00:13:46,583 --> 00:13:48,208
of the greatest engineer
and inventor

311
00:13:48,208 --> 00:13:50,000
that's basically ever existed.

312
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,125
[Nya] Are you talking about me?

313
00:13:51,125 --> 00:13:52,166
[Jay] Yeah!

314
00:13:52,166 --> 00:13:53,666
Was that not charming enough?

315
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:55,125
[Nya] You were
a selfish mercenary,

316
00:13:55,125 --> 00:13:56,291
like, three days ago.

317
00:13:56,291 --> 00:13:58,583
Sometimes I'm still not sure
how to take you.

318
00:13:58,583 --> 00:14:00,750
[Jay] That's fair. Now, go!

319
00:14:00,750 --> 00:14:02,708
[tires squealing]

320
00:14:04,416 --> 00:14:05,750
H'yah!

321
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:06,750
[Cole] Hi!

322
00:14:06,750 --> 00:14:08,250
Didn't expect you.

323
00:14:08,250 --> 00:14:09,541
Last I heard,
you got trapped in a cave.

324
00:14:09,541 --> 00:14:12,666
[Kai] No cave can keep me
from saving your bacon.

325
00:14:14,208 --> 00:14:15,833
What's crackin',
fellow fire people?

326
00:14:15,833 --> 00:14:16,833
Up top!

327
00:14:16,833 --> 00:14:17,833
[monsters snarling]

328
00:14:17,833 --> 00:14:19,083
Leave me hangin'?

329
00:14:19,083 --> 00:14:20,791
Uncool, fire bros!

330
00:14:22,708 --> 00:14:23,833
[snarling]

331
00:14:24,916 --> 00:14:28,000
The fault's not
in the parallel circuits.

332
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,250
[Nya] Percival! Here to help.

333
00:14:29,250 --> 00:14:30,166
Nya!

334
00:14:30,166 --> 00:14:31,666
Oh, man, we could use it.

335
00:14:31,666 --> 00:14:33,375
How did you get
inside the walls?

336
00:14:33,375 --> 00:14:34,500
Waste tunnels.

337
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:35,958
[inhaling] Still gross.

338
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:37,958
Beatrix could
send her monsters in that way!

339
00:14:37,958 --> 00:14:38,958
Doubt it.

340
00:14:38,958 --> 00:14:40,500
People like her
never even wonder

341
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:42,708
how people like us
take out their trash.

342
00:14:42,708 --> 00:14:43,875
What's wrong with the barrier?

343
00:14:43,875 --> 00:14:44,833
We don't know.

344
00:14:44,833 --> 00:14:46,791
We can't find any faults!

345
00:14:46,791 --> 00:14:48,125
I'll check the relays.

346
00:14:50,583 --> 00:14:52,041
[♪♪♪]

347
00:14:56,583 --> 00:14:57,625
[circuits crackling]

348
00:14:58,625 --> 00:14:59,666
[crackling]

349
00:15:04,333 --> 00:15:05,333
[Nya] What?

350
00:15:05,333 --> 00:15:06,541
Sabotage!

351
00:15:07,416 --> 00:15:10,666
[Loyalist]
All hail the Good Empress!

352
00:15:10,666 --> 00:15:12,333
[Nya grunts]

353
00:15:18,583 --> 00:15:19,916
[panting]

354
00:15:22,458 --> 00:15:23,875
[snarling]

355
00:15:23,875 --> 00:15:25,916
[gasping in fright]

356
00:15:29,125 --> 00:15:31,500
[screaming in panic]

357
00:15:35,458 --> 00:15:37,000
[snarling]

358
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,583
[screaming]

359
00:15:39,666 --> 00:15:41,500
[roaring]

360
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:43,083
[panicked screaming]

361
00:15:45,333 --> 00:15:46,750
[Riyu roars]

362
00:15:46,750 --> 00:15:47,625
[Wyldfyre cheers]

363
00:15:47,625 --> 00:15:48,625
[Frak] Thought we'd never find

364
00:15:48,625 --> 00:15:50,250
where these weirdos were headed.

365
00:15:50,250 --> 00:15:51,791
[Sora] Soon as I heard
the name "Beatrix,"

366
00:15:51,791 --> 00:15:53,875
it was pretty obvious.

367
00:15:53,875 --> 00:15:56,416
[♪♪♪]

368
00:15:56,416 --> 00:15:57,583
[monsters snarling]

369
00:15:57,583 --> 00:15:59,000
[Riyu roars]

370
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,833
[Frak] No offense, but so far,

371
00:16:00,833 --> 00:16:02,250
I'm not loving your hometown.

372
00:16:02,250 --> 00:16:03,833
[Sora] I've never been
a big fan either,

373
00:16:03,833 --> 00:16:04,916
but to be fair,

374
00:16:04,916 --> 00:16:06,708
it had fewer monsters
scaling the walls

375
00:16:06,708 --> 00:16:07,875
when I was a kid.

376
00:16:07,875 --> 00:16:10,416
Ah, it sounds like
it was boring back then.

377
00:16:10,416 --> 00:16:12,083
This rules!

378
00:16:12,083 --> 00:16:13,500
-[engine revving]
-[Sora] Look!

379
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:15,291
[Cole] Yaah! Yaah!

380
00:16:15,291 --> 00:16:16,291
-Kai!
-[Frak] Cole!

381
00:16:16,291 --> 00:16:18,333
Quit sitting around!

382
00:16:18,333 --> 00:16:20,208
Monster fight!

383
00:16:20,208 --> 00:16:22,625
H'yah! Y'ah! Hi-yah!

384
00:16:22,625 --> 00:16:24,208
[Frak] We're gonna
have to do that too, aren't we?

385
00:16:24,208 --> 00:16:25,625
[Sora] You are.

386
00:16:25,625 --> 00:16:26,750
I'm gonna go see

387
00:16:26,750 --> 00:16:28,000
if I can get
the city's defenses back up.

388
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,458
[Frak] Oh, cool.

389
00:16:29,458 --> 00:16:30,958
Good luck. [gulping nervously]

390
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:33,583
Whoa!

391
00:16:33,583 --> 00:16:34,833
Oh! Ooh-ho!

392
00:16:34,833 --> 00:16:35,875
Oh!

393
00:16:35,875 --> 00:16:37,333
Wah-ha!

394
00:16:37,333 --> 00:16:38,250
[gasping]

395
00:16:38,250 --> 00:16:39,958
Maybe nobody saw that.

396
00:16:39,958 --> 00:16:41,125
[Jay laughs]

397
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:42,708
Oh, man, kid!

398
00:16:42,708 --> 00:16:45,125
That was hilarious!

399
00:16:45,125 --> 00:16:46,125
[tires squealing]

400
00:16:46,125 --> 00:16:47,750
Ha ha. Yeah.

401
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:49,000
Meant to do it.

402
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,125
[Riyu roars]

403
00:16:51,125 --> 00:16:54,750
[Beatrix] The Ninja brought
a repulsive beast against me!

404
00:16:54,750 --> 00:16:55,916
[exasperated sighing]

405
00:16:55,916 --> 00:16:57,958
Please tell me
my dragon-draining facilities

406
00:16:57,958 --> 00:16:59,041
are still intact.

407
00:16:59,041 --> 00:17:00,916
The new senate
dismantled them,

408
00:17:00,916 --> 00:17:03,083
but I should be able
to make them functional again

409
00:17:03,083 --> 00:17:04,333
post haste.

410
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,333
Whoa-ho!

411
00:17:15,166 --> 00:17:16,375
[♪♪♪]

412
00:17:18,041 --> 00:17:19,625
[gasping]

413
00:17:23,541 --> 00:17:25,916
[whirring]

414
00:17:30,333 --> 00:17:31,375
[powering up]

415
00:17:31,375 --> 00:17:32,416
[Nya]
What's that supposed to--?

416
00:17:33,625 --> 00:17:34,750
[panting]

417
00:17:35,750 --> 00:17:37,416
[cutting]

418
00:17:37,416 --> 00:17:38,583
[Nya] No!

419
00:17:38,583 --> 00:17:41,625
Beatrix will be able
to breach the city walls!

420
00:17:44,666 --> 00:17:46,041
[cracking joints]

421
00:17:48,625 --> 00:17:49,625
[Sora] Aah!

422
00:17:49,625 --> 00:17:50,791
[distant screaming]

423
00:17:50,791 --> 00:17:53,000
[Sora] That doesn't sound good.

424
00:17:54,791 --> 00:17:55,875
[device thudding]

425
00:17:55,875 --> 00:17:57,041
[Nya] H'yah!

426
00:17:59,916 --> 00:18:02,583
[Nya] Sora?
Where'd you come from?

427
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:04,583
[Sora] Long story,

428
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:06,166
but me, Frak,
Wyldfyre, and Riyu

429
00:18:06,166 --> 00:18:07,916
ended up in a place
with unexpected kittens,

430
00:18:07,916 --> 00:18:09,208
then we jumped
through a fountain

431
00:18:09,208 --> 00:18:10,458
to where Frak's dad was,

432
00:18:10,458 --> 00:18:12,750
but a man in a big hat
made us wear some shame boards.

433
00:18:12,750 --> 00:18:14,041
[Nya]
Maybe I have a concussion,

434
00:18:14,041 --> 00:18:16,250
'cause that sounded like
a bunch of nonsense.

435
00:18:16,250 --> 00:18:17,291
[Sora] It was.

436
00:18:17,291 --> 00:18:18,333
Why are we running?

437
00:18:19,333 --> 00:18:20,458
[Nya] To stop them!

438
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:23,000
[Nya] Are your powers working?

439
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,708
'Cause we could use them
right now!

440
00:18:24,708 --> 00:18:26,916
[Sora] Wait,
are your powers wonky too?

441
00:18:26,916 --> 00:18:28,625
[Nya] I think everyone's are!

442
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,041
[cutting]

443
00:18:32,041 --> 00:18:34,083
[Sora] Well, worth a shot.

444
00:18:34,083 --> 00:18:36,833
Please work, please work...

445
00:18:36,833 --> 00:18:39,791
[♪♪♪]

446
00:18:39,791 --> 00:18:41,250
Yes!

447
00:18:41,250 --> 00:18:42,333
I think I--

448
00:18:44,166 --> 00:18:46,541
That's not what I was trying--

449
00:18:46,541 --> 00:18:47,541
[Nya] Take the win!

450
00:18:47,541 --> 00:18:48,708
Come on!

451
00:18:49,791 --> 00:18:52,875
[Riyu roars]

452
00:18:52,875 --> 00:18:55,000
[yelping]

453
00:18:59,333 --> 00:19:00,916
[Kai] H'yah!

454
00:19:02,250 --> 00:19:03,750
[snarling]

455
00:19:04,958 --> 00:19:06,583
[Wyldfyre]
Great news, everybody!

456
00:19:06,583 --> 00:19:07,583
Me!

457
00:19:07,583 --> 00:19:09,083
Yee-haw!

458
00:19:09,083 --> 00:19:10,166
[monster snarling]

459
00:19:10,166 --> 00:19:11,583
[Kai] H'yah!

460
00:19:12,583 --> 00:19:14,541
I know you missed me.

461
00:19:14,541 --> 00:19:16,625
[Kai] Well, on a scale
from zero to fire!

462
00:19:16,625 --> 00:19:19,500
Jay and my sister are below zero
on the fun scale!

463
00:19:19,500 --> 00:19:20,791
[Cole] H'ah! H'yah!

464
00:19:20,791 --> 00:19:23,375
[snarling]

465
00:19:23,375 --> 00:19:24,541
H'yah!

466
00:19:24,541 --> 00:19:26,041
[snarling]

467
00:19:26,041 --> 00:19:27,375
[Cole] Frak! Hey, man,

468
00:19:27,375 --> 00:19:28,416
probably not the best time,

469
00:19:28,416 --> 00:19:29,666
but I'm so sorry about
how I acted

470
00:19:29,666 --> 00:19:30,708
when those specters--

471
00:19:30,708 --> 00:19:32,041
[Frak] Forgiven!

472
00:19:32,041 --> 00:19:33,958
There are a lot more kinds
of elemental monsters here

473
00:19:33,958 --> 00:19:35,000
than in Umbrasylvis.

474
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,833
[Cole] Yeah, what--
what's an Umbrasylvis?

475
00:19:37,833 --> 00:19:39,333
[tires squealing]

476
00:19:43,375 --> 00:19:45,500
[♪♪♪]

477
00:19:48,083 --> 00:19:49,541
-[tires squealing]
-[Jay] H'yah!

478
00:19:49,541 --> 00:19:51,291
[screeching]

479
00:19:51,291 --> 00:19:52,416
[tires squealing]

480
00:19:53,375 --> 00:19:55,041
[snarling]

481
00:19:56,416 --> 00:19:58,083
[Jay] Wipers!
Where are the wipers?

482
00:20:03,875 --> 00:20:05,250
[Jay yelps]

483
00:20:06,541 --> 00:20:07,625
[grunting]

484
00:20:11,916 --> 00:20:13,291
[powering up]

485
00:20:13,291 --> 00:20:14,291
[cutting]

486
00:20:18,125 --> 00:20:19,250
[Nya grunts]

487
00:20:21,166 --> 00:20:22,291
[Sora] Yaah!

488
00:20:32,166 --> 00:20:34,041
[Nya] Can you try
to shut it down again?

489
00:20:34,041 --> 00:20:36,500
[Sora] Come on,
one more time...

490
00:20:42,333 --> 00:20:43,791
No!

491
00:20:48,166 --> 00:20:49,208
[slamming]

492
00:20:49,208 --> 00:20:50,458
Oh no!

493
00:20:50,458 --> 00:20:53,208
[Riyu roars weakly]

494
00:20:53,208 --> 00:20:54,875
[Beatrix] Forget that beast!

495
00:20:54,875 --> 00:20:56,500
You must climb the walls!

496
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:58,416
We cannot be kept out!

497
00:20:58,416 --> 00:20:59,916
[wall segment slamming]

498
00:21:01,541 --> 00:21:02,583
Empress,

499
00:21:02,583 --> 00:21:04,541
your Loyalists inside the walls

500
00:21:04,541 --> 00:21:06,083
have not disappointed.

501
00:21:06,083 --> 00:21:08,333
[Beatrix] They will be thrilled
at my return.

502
00:21:08,333 --> 00:21:09,333
Advance!

503
00:21:09,333 --> 00:21:11,250
[monsters roaring]

504
00:21:16,791 --> 00:21:19,250
[Cole] Waah!

505
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:20,250
[monsters snarling]

506
00:21:20,250 --> 00:21:21,333
[Cole] Head for that wall--

507
00:21:21,333 --> 00:21:22,375
[grunting]

508
00:21:24,083 --> 00:21:25,875
[monsters roaring]

509
00:21:33,583 --> 00:21:35,333
[Beatrix] Imperium!

510
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:39,416
I have returned!

511
00:21:39,416 --> 00:21:41,041
[♪♪♪]

512
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:45,916
[♪♪♪]

